  "vacancy_language": "en",
  "text": "<p class=\"location\">Location: <strong>Hybrid role in Dublin, Ireland or London, UK</strong></p><h3 class=\"company-description\">Company</h3><p>%hirify_global% develops XpertOS, an agentic SaaS product that integrates AI agents into a customer engagement platform.</p><h3 class=\"what-you-will-do\">What you will do</h3><ul><li>Build and release customer-facing XpertOS features in Python from customer problem discovery through testing and deployment.</li><li>Work with the product team to shape feature scope, priorities, specifications, and shippable increments.</li><li>Use AI coding agents throughout planning, development, testing, and code review.</li><li>Build and improve LLM-powered agents, including prompts, tools, retrieval, and evaluation.</li><li>Plan, test, document, and deploy maintainable code while learning and using AWS services supporting XpertOS.</li><li>Contribute to shared agent skills, workflows, guardrails, tooling, and development practices.</li></ul><h3 class=\"requirements\">Requirements</h3><ul><li>1–3 years of professional experience building Python applications.</li><li>Professional proficiency with agentic development and regular use of AI coding agents such as Claude Code, Cursor, or Copilot agents, including the ability to explain how reliable results are achieved.</li><li>Product mindset focused on customer needs, outcomes, and the purpose behind features.</li><li>Strong interest in agentic SaaS, LLMs, and customer-facing applications.</li><li>Sound fundamentals in testing, version control, code review, and maintainable software development.</li><li>Excellent analytical and problem-solving skills.</li><li>Clear written and spoken communication with technical and non-technical people.</li><li>Ability to work independently and as part of a team.</li><li><strong>Ability to work in the hybrid Dublin or London setup.</strong></li></ul><h3 class=\"nice-to-have\">Nice to have</h3><ul><li>Hands-on experience with LLM APIs, agent frameworks, retrieval/RAG, or LLM evaluation.</li><li>Side projects, open-source work, or independently shipped products, especially agentic projects.</li><li>Experience with AWS services such as Lambda, Bedrock, or Cognito.</li><li>Exposure to product discovery, including user interviews, specification writing, or backlog prioritization.</li><li>Familiarity with ClickHouse or SQL analytics.</li></ul><h3 class=\"culture-benefits\">Culture &amp; Benefits</h3><ul><li>Hybrid work in Dublin, Ireland or London, UK.</li><li>AI coding agents are an integral part of the development workflow.</li><li>Opportunity to influence product direction, tooling, workflows, and development practices.</li><li>Ideas and input are valued from the outset.</li></ul><h3 class=\"hiring-process\">Hiring process</h3><ul><li>The interview explores experience with AI agents, approaches to product challenges, and technical experience.</li></ul>",
  "tldr": "Python Developer (AI) (Python/LLM Agents): Building customer-facing features and LLM-powered agents for XpertOS, an agentic SaaS product, with an accent on product thinking, AI coding agents, retrieval, prompts, tools, and evaluation. Focus on designing reliable agent workflows, developing and testing Python functionality, and shaping solutions around customer needs.",
